$q+=,@('                    <div class="drill-scenario"><h5>Q7: What is the shared responsibility model for compliance in managed K8s?</h5><ol><li>Customer handles everything</li><li>Cloud provider certifies control plane (FedRAMP/SOC2); customer certifies their workloads (RBAC, encryption, audit)</li><li>Cloud provider handles all compliance</li><li>CNCF certifies the cluster</li></ol></div>','                    <div class="drill-solution"><details><summary>✅ Answer</summary><p><strong>Answer: 2. Split responsibility.</strong> AWS/Azure/GCP certify the managed control plane. YOU must certify: pod security, RBAC, NetworkPolicies, etcd encryption, audit logging, and your application security controls.</p></details></div>')
$q+=,@('                    <div class="drill-scenario"><h5>Q8: What does GDPR require for personal data breach notification?</h5><ol><li>No notification required</li><li>Notify supervisory authority within 72 hours of becoming aware of the breach</li><li>Notify within 30 days</li><li>Only notify if data is financial</li></ol></div>','                    <div class="drill-solution"><details><summary>✅ Answer</summary><p><strong>Answer: 2. 72-hour notification.</strong> GDPR Article 33 requires notifying the relevant data protection authority within 72 hours of discovering a personal data breach. This makes audit logging and incident detection critical for compliance.</p></details></div>')
